producerDescription = "If you are looking for a rosé that is light pink, light in flavor, and slightly sweet… this wine is not for you. Drawing more inspiration from Tavel than Provence, our Dry Rosé tends to the darker and more structured side with bramble fruit aromatics to complement its bigger body. While still enjoyable on its own, this is a Rosé that we hope has a place at the dining table all four seasons of the year. Song Pairing: “Qualified” by Dr. John"
